{% block block_designer_product_slider %}
    {% set title = block.slots.getSlot('sliderTitle') %}
    {% set description = block.slots.getSlot('sliderDescription') %}
    {% set products = block.slots.getSlot('sliderProducts') %}
    {% set columns = 1 %}

    <div class="col-12 header-section">
        <div class="row justify-content-center text-center">
            <div class="col-12 col-md-8">
                {% if title %}
                    <div class="slider-main-title" data-cms-element-id="{{ title.id }}">
                        {% sw_include '@Storefront/storefront/element/cms-element-' ~ title.type ~ '.html.twig' with {
                            element: title
                        } %}
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                {# Legacy blocks still render until opened and saved with the new heading editor. #}
                {% if description and (not title or title.type != 'designer-slider-header') %}
                    <div class="slider-main-description mt-2" data-cms-element-id="{{ description.id }}">
                        {% sw_include '@Storefront/storefront/element/cms-element-' ~ description.type ~ '.html.twig' with {
                            element: description
                        } %}
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {% if products %}
        {#
            OPTIONAL EXAMPLE ONLY — hide descriptions in this slider:

            Add hideDescription: true alongside element: products in the include
            below. Twig includes inherit context, so the flag reaches the product
            card through cms-element-product-slider.html.twig and card/box.html.twig.

            Example include arguments:
                element: products,
                hideDescription: true

            Then in component/product/card/box-standard.html.twig, replace the
            existing description block call with:

                {% if not hideDescription|default(false) %}
                    {{ block('component_product_box_description') }}
                {% endif %}

            Both changes are needed. Other sliders do not pass the flag and keep
            their descriptions. For different card styling, add a unique class
            such as designer-product-slider to this wrapper and scope SCSS under
            .designer-product-slider .product-box.box-standard. The existing
            .product-box.box-standard styles currently affect all standard cards.

            OPTIONAL: hiding other sections or adding content to this slider only:

            Pass another flag alongside element: products in the include below:
                isDesignerSlider: true

            Inside our card/box-standard.html.twig override, wrap individual calls
            to hide them only when this flag is present. For example, replace the
            existing rating call (inside its product.ratingAverage condition) with:

                {% if not isDesignerSlider|default(false) %}
                    {{ block('component_product_box_rating') }}
                {% endif %}

            The same approach works for description, variant characteristics,
            price or action calls. Wrap the existing call instead of adding a
            second copy. Removing the action removes the card's buying controls.

            To add a banner ABOVE the image, add this block override to our
            card/box-standard.html.twig file:

                {% block component_product_box_image %}
                    {% if isDesignerSlider|default(false) %}
                        <div class="designer-card-banner">Special offer</div>
                    {% endif %}
                    {{ parent() }}
                {% endblock %}

            Keep parent() so Shopware still renders the image and wishlist.
            Alternatively, put conditional custom markup directly into our
            product-info div, for example after the product-name block call:

                {% if isDesignerSlider|default(false) %}
                    <p class="designer-card-note">Exclusive selection</p>
                {% endif %}

            These example texts are static. Use a snippet for translated text,
            a product custom field for product-specific data, or a registered
            CMS config field when editors need to change it per slider.
            A Twig flag alone does not create an Administration setting.

            Added content must fit the fixed 460px card or its height must change.
            A banner above the image also moves it down: update the scoped
            .stretched-link::after height to cover that extra banner height.
            Other sliders keep their original output because the flag is absent.

            This comment does not enable any of these changes.
        #}
        <div class="col-12 product-slider-wrapper mt-5" data-cms-element-id="{{ products.id }}">
            {% sw_include '@Storefront/storefront/element/cms-element-' ~ products.type ~ '.html.twig' with {
                element: products
            } %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
